Author:     Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Sat Nov 14 20:22:28 2026 -0500
Commit:     Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 15 18:07:09 2026 -0500

    media: qcom: camss: consume saved completions after gen1 idle ack
    
    A gen1 IRQ can snapshot both REG_UPDATE and WM_DONE. When REG_UPDATE
    acknowledges a STOPPING output, it returns the deferred final buffer and
    can install fresh pending buffers. Dispatching WM_DONE from the same
    saved status then reports "Missing ready buf" on the idle output or
    consumes a newly installed buffer using a completion from the old stream.
    
    Keep the idle acknowledgment before returning the final buffer. Capture
    the old WM indices under output_lock and return that mask from the ISR
    reg_update callback. Consume only those WM completions and the matching
    PIX composite completion from this saved IRQ status in the 4.1, 4.7 and
    4.8 dispatchers. Keep unrelated and later completions active. Update the
    17x callback to return zero without changing its acknowledgment behavior.
    
    Native MSM8926 tracing established the callback order before this fix.
    An extracted production-function model passes 84 sanitizer executions
    and fifteen baseline/unsafe-alternative controls on this media base.
    The complete ARM CAMSS component builds with W=1 and KCFI under
    COMPILE_TEST. This does not establish a patched hardware boot or native
    ARM32 support under the current IOMMU_DMA Kconfig dependency.
    
    Codex (OpenAI) assisted with native trace analysis, fix and regression
    drafting, build/CFI checks and this description during Fx0 bringup.
    
    Fixes: 4c98a5f57f90 ("media: camss: Add VFE files")

